[D Forever Alliance 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Built 24 Sep 2026 from the Wowhead Forever atlas + Questie Classic data.\\Every step carries explicit coordinates because the Forever quest DB is empty. 17 Oct 2026: added Grund and Gozwin (97277, new in a later beta build).]
[GA Dwarf]
[OC]|cffffffffColdridge Valley 1-6|r  -  the Dwarf start (Shaman or Hunter). Class-only lines are hidden for the other class; the Human start is its own chapter.
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear rule:|r slow 2H mace/axe/staff for damage (Forever's Dwarf racial Mace Specialization = crit with maces). Leather until Mail at 40. Stats: weapon dps > Str > Int > Agi > Sta.
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear rule (Hunter):|r your ranged weapon IS the class - its dps beats everything else on this list. Then Agility (2 ranged attack power and crit per point, and your pet copies your crit), then plain attack power, then Stamina. Leather until Mail at 40. The melee weapon is only a stat stick. Guns the whole way on this route, so one ammo type: starting gun -> Ornate Blunderbuss (vendor, 4) -> Daryl's Hunting Rifle (quest, 13) -> |cff66ff66Calibrated Blunderbuss|r (Hall of Thanes quest, 16). Buy a Small Shot Pouch (+10% ranged attack speed) at the first gunsmith and never run below 200 shot.
[OC]|cffffcc00Professions (Forever):|r |cff66ff66Skinning + Mining first|r, plus First Aid + Cooking. Why not Leatherworking yet: Forever's new levelling sets - Totemic Leather (Str/Sta/Int + spell power) and Brawler's Leather (Str/Agi/Sta) - mostly need Pristine Leather, a Scarce reagent (belt 2, gloves 2, boots 3, hood 4, tunic 6, leggings 8; players report ~1 per 600 skins, and reportedly it stops once your character passes 25 - beta player testing, Blizzard has not commented), so skin everything, count it and decide at 25: 4 = belt + gloves, 25 = all six (the level-25 note at the top of 25-26 Duskwood has the switch). The exception, and the real prize: |cff66ff66Totemic Leather Armor|r (chest, req 15, +7 Str +3 Sta +3 Int +6 spell) and |cff66ff66Totemic Leather Pants|r (req 20, +9 Str +4 Sta +4 Int +7 spell) need NO Pristine Leather - only leather, hides and 1 / 2 Sulfuric Acid - and beat every chest and legs in the 15-30 guide, but their patterns are tradeable dungeon drops (added 31 Oct; which dungeon and how often is unknown), so they are an Auction House question: the guide searches the AH for "Totemic Leather" at every city pass and switches you to Leatherworking the moment one is affordable. Until then Mining makes the gold and its veins drop Pyrite, the other new reagent - bank every Pyrite (6 cover the Armor and Pants acid), and bank your Light Leather too (the Armor alone is 16, and skilling to 75 eats more). Passives: Skinning = +5% damage to Beasts and Dragonkin (stacks with Big Game Hunter), Mining = +5% total health, Cooking = eating a cooked food for 10 seconds gives Well Fed for 15 min: a stat buff plus +5% XP from kills (the same +5% on every food, so the stat is what matters), First Aid now makes the healing potions (Alchemy no longer does). Junior Mining/Skinning trainers stand in Anvilmar, so you gather from level 2.
[OC]|cffffcc00Cooking + Fishing plan (Forever):|r your food ladder is Roasted Boar Meat (+1 Str, trainer) -> |cff66ff66Longjaw Mud Snapper (+10 attack power, level 5+)|r -> |cff66ff66Mithril Head Trout (+20 attack power, level 25+)|r. Both fish come from your own fishing rod, so Fishing is part of this guide: learn it at Paxton Ganter (Iceflow Lake, level 8), buy Khara Deepwater's Strong Fishing Pole (+45 Fishing in Forever) at the loch at 12, and fish where the guide says "fish to N". Skill targets: Cooking 50 by 12 (Journeyman at Daryl Riknussun, Ironforge), 80 by 16, 125 by 24 (Expert Cookbook from Shandrina, Ashenvale), 175 by ~30 for the trout; Fishing 25 by 12, 50 by 15 (Journeyman at Grimnur Stonebrand, Ironforge), 100 by 22, 130+ by 28. Every other recipe on the route is a skill-up filler: cook whatever meat you loot and eat the best thing you have.
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Professions (Hunter):|r same answer - Skinning + Mining, unless you want Leatherworking anyway. Brawler's Leather (Str/Agi/Sta) is your set (skip the Totemic pieces) and it has the same Pristine Leather gate (4 for belt + gloves, 25 for all six), with Shadowgem from tin and copper veins in place of the acid - so Mining feeds it too; bank the Shadowgems. Skinning's +5% vs Beasts stacks with Big Game Hunter. Cooking matters twice for you: your own food buff and cheap pet food (boars and bears eat bread, cheese, fish, fruit, fungus and meat).
[OC]|cffffcc00Camping (Forever):|r Cooking 1 teaches the Basic Campfire (3 object slots). Sit or craft at a fire for 1 minute to get its buffs (1 hour). Each player adds ONE profession object: your Lodestone (Mining 20) = melee attack power, your Camp Chair (Skinning 20) = +2% crit, First Aid Kit = stamina, Fish Bowl (Fishing 20; does not stack with Blessing of Kings) = +8% all stats, Leatherworking tent = rested XP. Objects have a 1-hour cooldown and the fire vanishes after ~10-15 min, so set camp right before a dungeon or a long grind, with your friend adding his object. The Camping 101 quests (level 6, Eric Brighthammer) teach the tier-1 objects once that skill is 20.
[OC]|cffffcc00Launch rule (1-6):|r no shared tags in Forever - on a camped named mob (Grik'nir, the Snow Leopard Prowler) INVITE the people standing there (kill credit shares in a party; most drop items don't). If no group forms in ~2 min, tick the step and keep moving; the catch-up line at the tunnel brings you back. Expect the first 10-20 min to be the worst: in 2019 the Coldridge crowd thinned 10-20 minutes after the first wave reached Grik'nir.

